# Canonical game icon build integration

Require at least one canonical `.ico` under `game/` in the game manifest and
feed repository-generated icon outputs into Unreal staging and packaging through
the same hermetic build evidence as every other generated input.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Treat zero canonical game icons as invalid source evidence during the
  supported preflight.
- [ ] Consume the final repository-owned icon producer under `src/unreal/icon`
  without duplicating or bypassing that producer inside `tools/build/`.
- [ ] Record generated icon identities, paths, hashes, and target-specific
  transformations in build evidence before Unreal or platform packaging uses
  them.
- [ ] Make `tools/build/run.py` consume only validated generated icon outputs for
  the selected platforms; do not reach into arbitrary host or editor caches.
- [ ] Keep intermediate icon conversion output under the canonical `.cache/`
  workspace and publish only the platform-native icon data required by the
  final package.

## Dependencies

Depends on build preflight, the canonical build runner, and completion of the
repository-owned icon producer. This record does not own or modify that producer.

## Evidence

Add manifest, generated-icon, Unreal staging, and packaged-target validation
evidence here once integration lands.
